====Noun====
{{en-noun|children|childer|pl2qual=dialectal or archaic}}

# {{senseid|en|kid aged 0 to 18 years}} {{lb|en|[[Appendix:Glossary#broadly|broadly]]}} A [[person]] who has not yet reached [[adulthood]], whether [[natural]] ([[puberty]]), [[cultural]] ([[initiation]]), or [[legal]] ([[majority]]).
#: {{syn|en|kid}}
#: {{hypo|en|newborn|neonate|preteen|adolescent|tweenager|teenager|tween|teen|preadult}}
#: {{ux|en|Go easy on him: he is but a '''child'''.}}
#* '''2003''' Powerpuff Girls: 'Twas the Fight Before Christmas (narration)
#*: {{quote|en|And not just the '''children''', teenagers too. Chuck wants a football, Kathleen a tattoo.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-07|author=w:Joseph Stiglitz|volume=188|issue=26|page=19|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly|title=Globalisation is about taxes too|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/2013/may/27/globalisation-is-about-taxes-too|passage=It is time the international community faced the reality: we have an unmanageable, unfair, distortionary global tax regime. {{...}} It is the starving of the public sector which has been pivotal in America no longer being the land of opportunity – with a '''child''''s life prospects more dependent on the income and education of its parents than in other advanced countries.}}
## {{senseid|en|kid aged 1 to 11 years}} {{lb|en|[[pediatrics]]|sometimes, in a [[Appendix:Glossary#strict|stricter]] sense}} A kid aged 1 to 11 years, whereas [[neonate#Noun|neonates]] are aged 0 to 1 month, [[infant#Noun|infants]] are aged 1 month to 12 months, and [[adolescent#Noun|adolescents]] are aged 12 years to 18 years.
##: {{ux|en|Regular chores can be appropriate for both '''children''' and adolescents, given age-appropriate limits on difficulty level and time on task.}}
##: {{hyper|en|kid}}
##: {{cot|en|newborn|neonate|infant|adolescent|teenager|teen}}
# {{senseid|en|offspring of any age including adulthood}} {{lb|en|with possessive}} One's [[direct]] [[descendant]] by [[birth]], regardless of [[age]]; one's [[offspring]]; a [[son]] or [[daughter]].
#: {{ux|en|My youngest '''child''' is forty-three this year.}}
#: {{ux|en|His adult '''children''' visit him yearly.}}
# {{senseid|en|cartomancy}} {{lb|en|cartomancy}} The thirteenth [[Lenormand]] card.
# {{senseid|en|figuratively, of times or tribes}} {{lb|en|figurative}} A [[figurative]] [[offspring]], ''particularly:''
## A person considered a [[product]] of a [[place]] or [[culture]], a [[member]] of a [[tribe]] or culture, regardless of age.
##: {{ux|en|The '''children''' of Israel.}}
##: {{ux|en|He is a '''child''' of his times.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1984|author=[[w:Mary Jane Phillips-Matz|Mary Jane Matz]]|title=The Many Lives of Otto Kahn: A Biography|page=5|passage=For more than forty years, he preached the creed of art and beauty. He was heir to the ancient wisdom of Israel, a '''child''' of Germany, a subject of Great Britain, later an American citizen, but in truth a citizen of the world.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=[[w:Edward Plunkett, 18th Baron of Dunsany|Edward John Moreton Dunsany]]|title={{w|The Last Book of Wonder|Tales of Wonder}}|page=64|passage=Plash-Goo was of the '''children''' of the giants, whose sire was Uph. And the lineage of Uph had dwindled in bulk for the last five hundred years, till the giants were now no more than fifteen foot high; but Uph ate elephants{{...}}}}
## {{senseid|en|figuratively, derived or caused}} Anything [[derive]]d from or [[cause]]d by something.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=w:Salman Rushdie| title={{w|Midnight's Children|Midnight's '''Children'''}}| passage=Poverty, disease, and despair are the '''children''' of war.}}
## {{senseid|en|child element in computing}} {{lb|en|computing}} A [[data]] [[item]], [[process]], or [[object]] which has a [[subservient]] or [[derivative]] [[role]] relative to another.
##: {{ux|en|The '''child''' node then stores the actual data of the parent node.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=John Mongan; Noah Kindler; Eric Giguère|title=Programming Interviews Exposed
|passage=The algorithm pops the stack to obtain a new current node when there are no more '''children''' (when it reaches a leaf).}}
# {{senseid|en|childe, youth of noble birth}} {{alt form|en|childe||youth of noble birth}}
# {{senseid|en|mathematics}} {{lb|en|mathematics|programming}} A subordinate [[node]] of a [[tree]].
# {{senseid|en|female child, obsoletely}} {{lb|en|obsolete|specifically}} A [[female]] child, a [[girl]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Winter's Tale|III|iii|288|2|passage=A boy, or a '''Childe''' I wonder?}}

